{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetNQpJ3B84bwQTcRtugA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-16` — Order entity, no status field yet\n- `OrderController.kt:21-34` — POST /orders endpoint exists; GET endpoints at :36-45\n- `OrderRepository.kt` — in-memory store with save, findById, existsById, findAll\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` — Shipment has status field with enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — POST /shipments creates with CREATED status\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` — in-memory store, methods to find/save/list shipments\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — centralized exception→response mapping\n\n**Conventions this repository already follows:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler maps to status + ApiError body\n- Repositories are in-memory (ConcurrentHashMap), not persisted\n- Tests check both HTTP status and error body (code, message, fields)\n- Endpoints return ResponseEntity with appropriate HttpStatus\n- All errors go through the error envelope (not free-form responses)\n\n**Affected files — why they cannot be avoided:**\n1. `Order.kt` — must add status field and OrderStatus enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` — must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` — must add method to find shipments by orderId (to check confirmations) and support cancellation\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add method to find all shipments for an order\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — must validate order is not CANCELLED before creating shipment\n6. `ApiError.kt` — must add error codes for new conflict cases\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for cancel endpoint and edge cases\n8. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add test for creating shipment on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Cascade cancellation: must not partially succeed (all shipments cancel together with order)\n- Idempotency: repeated cancel of already-CANCELLED order must succeed, not fail\n- Atomicity: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, cancel must fail and leave order/shipments untouched\n- Existing tests must not break when Order gains a status field\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What error codes to use for the two new 409 cases? (order with confirmed shipment, shipment for cancelled order) → Will add SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and ORDER_CANCELLED to ErrorCode enum\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — Add method `findShipmentsByOrderId(orderId)` to find all shipments for an order, and `updateOrderStatus(orderId, status)` to change order status.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add method `findByOrderId(orderId)` to return all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt** — Add two ErrorCode values: `SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED` (order cannot be cancelled if any shipment is confirmed) and `ORDER_CANCELLED` (cannot create shipment for cancelled order).\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** — Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED if any shipment is CONFIRMED (and changes nothing)\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, succeeds (idempotent) and returns the order unchanged\n   - If order is ACTIVE, sets status to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, and returns the cancelled order\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** — Modify POST /shipments to check if order is CANCELLED before creating; throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) if so.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order successfully\n   - Cancel idempotently (already CANCELLED order)\n   - Reject cancel when order has CONFIRMED shipment (409, SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED)\n   - Reject cancel of non-existent order (404)\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test: reject creating shipment for CANCELLED order (409, ORDER_CANCELLED).\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could have added a separate service layer for cancellation logic, but the existing code uses repository pattern directly in controllers, so adding the logic there is consistent.\n- Could have stored a reference to ShipmentRepository in OrderController without injecting it, but Spring's dependency injection pattern requires constructor injection for testability.\n- Could have used a single generic ErrorCode like VALIDATION_FAILED for all new 409 cases, but the existing pattern has specific codes (ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS), so specific codes maintain consistency.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order (happy path):**\n   - Input: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel (no body)\n   - Fetch order from repository\n   - Fetch all shipments for that order\n   - Check: if any shipment.status == CONFIRMED → throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED), nothing changes\n   - Update order.status = CANCELLED\n   - For each shipment with status == CREATED, update shipment.status = CANCELLED\n   - Return 200 with updated Order\n   - Call: OrderRepository.save(), ShipmentRepository.save() (for each shipment)\n\n2. **Cancel already-CANCELLED order (idempotent):**\n   - Same as above but order.status is already CANCELLED\n   - Skip \"update order status\" (already CANCELLED)\n   - Return 200 with order (unchanged)\n\n3. **Cancel order that doesn't exist:**\n   - Fetch order → null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n   - Response: 404 with error envelope\n\n4. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - Fetch order and shipments\n   - Detect CONFIRMED shipment\n   - Throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED, \"Cannot cancel order with confirmed shipment\")\n   - No changes to database\n   - Response: 409 with error envelope\n\n5. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order:**\n   - Input: POST /shipments with orderId for a CANCELLED order\n   - Fetch order (or just status check via repository)\n   - Detect order.status == CANCELLED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, \"Cannot create shipment for cancelled order\")\n   - Response: 409 with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest.kt:**\n   - `cancelActiveOrder()` — create order, call cancel, verify 200, order.status = CANCELLED\n   - `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrder()` — cancel twice, second call returns 200, order unchanged\n   - `cancelOrderWithConfirmedShipment()` — create order + confirmed shipment, cancel → 409 SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED, order stays ACTIVE\n   - `cancelNonExistentOrder()` — call cancel on unknown orderId → 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - `cancelCasacadesCancelledShipments()` — create order + CREATED shipment, cancel → shipment status becomes CANCELLED\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt:**\n   - `rejectCreateShipmentForCancelledOrder()` — cancel order, try to create shipment → 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378,"cache_read_input_tokens":23885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10ea990f-efad-4608-abf7-1400d09d1bee","uuid":"0d06fd56-bcea-4359-867f-8a31caa36314","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:52:26.959Z","request_id":"req_011CetNQoeai4ZkQaoqBvW2d"}
