ntControllerTest, CustomerControllerTest, and SampleServiceApplicationTests all pass without modification (except for added cleanup in the reset() methods to clear shipmentRepository when needed).\n\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels active order, persists it, and cascades to CREATED shipments** — Test `cancelActiveOrder()` verifies successful cancel returns 200 with CANCELLED status. Test `cancelCasacadesCancelledShipments()` verifies CREATED shipments are cascaded to CANCELLED status.\n\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with rest of API** — New errors use ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) via the existing GlobalExceptionHandler pattern. Added SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and ORDER_CANCELLED to ErrorCode enum following the existing naming convention (ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, etc.).\n\n5. ✅ **Repeated cancel succeeds; confirmed shipment blocks; unknown order rejected; cancelled order rejects shipments** — Tests cover:\n   - `cancel is idempotent` — calling cancel twice on CANCELLED order returns 200 both times\n   - `cancel returns 409 when order has confirmed shipment` — verified 409 SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED thrown and order stays ACTIVE\n   - `cancel returns 404 for non-existent order` — verified 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - `rejectCreateShipmentForCancelledOrder()` — verified creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — Only modified existing Kotlin/Spring files, no pom.xml changes.\n\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only changed:\n   - Order.kt (added status field and OrderStatus enum)\n   - OrderController.kt (added cancel endpoint and imported ShipmentRepository)\n   - OrderRepository.kt (unchanged in structure, no methods added, works as-is)\n   - ShipmentRepository.kt (added findByOrderId() method to find shipments by orderId)\n   - ShipmentController.kt (added order cancellation check)\n   - ApiError.kt (added error codes)\n   - Test files (added tests for new functionality)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **Order.kt** — Added OrderStatus enum and status field with default ACTIVE. This is backward-compatible because the default keeps new orders in ACTIVE state.\n\n- **OrderController.kt** — Added ShipmentRepository dependency injection and POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint. Logic correctly:\n  - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n  - Returns idempotently (200) if already CANCELLED\n  - Throws 409 SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED if any shipment is CONFIRMED (atomic, no changes)\n  - Cascades cancellation to CREATED shipments\n  - Returns 200 with cancelled order\n\n- **ShipmentController.kt** — Added OrderRepository dependency injection and validates order is not CANCELLED before creating shipment. Correctly throws 409 ORDER_CANCELLED.\n\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId(orderId) method, a simple filter operation, no side effects.\n\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added two error codes (SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED, ORDER_CANCELLED) following existing enum pattern.\n\n- **Test files** — Added 6 new tests to OrderControllerTest covering all cancel scenarios, and 1 test to ShipmentControllerTest for the cancelled order validation. All tests follow existing patterns (MockMvc, jsonPath assertions).\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. The implementation fully addresses all requirements:\n- Order status lifecycle (ACTIVE → CANCELLED) ✅\n- Idempotent cancellation ✅\n- All-or-nothing constraint with CONFIRMED shipments ✅\n- Cascading CREATED shipment cancellation ✅\n- Preventing shipment creation for cancelled orders ✅\n- Proper error codes and HTTP status codes ✅\n- No new dependencies ✅\n- All existing and new tests passing ✅\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint managing order status (ACTIVE/CANCELLED) with idempotent cancellation, cascading shipment cancellation, and validation preventing cancellation if any shipment is confirmed.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field to Order\n              OrderController.kt — Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with full cancel logic\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId() to query shipments by order ID\n              ShipmentController.kt — Added validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders\n              ApiError.kt — Added SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 6 new tests: status check, active cancel, idempotent cancel, 404 unknown, 409 confirmed shipment, cascade CREATED shipments\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 1 test: reject shipment creation for cancelled order\n\nTests         newly created order has ACTIVE status — verifies default status\n              cancels an active order and returns 200 with CANCELLED status — happy path\n              cancel is idempotent - cancelling already cancelled order succeeds — idempotency\n              cancel returns 404 for non-existent order — 404 case\n              cancel returns 409 when order has confirmed shipment and changes nothing — 409 atomic case\n              cancel cascades to CREATED shipments — verifies cascade behavior\n              rejectCreateShipmentForCancelledOrder — verifies shipment creation validation\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 20 tests (10 OrderControllerTest, 6 ShipmentControllerTest, 3 CustomerControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests), 0 failures\n\nNot done      None — all acceptance criteria met and all tests passing\n```","ttft_ms":4295,"type":"result","duration_ms":210836,"uuid":"43f4c7f4-fa14-4404-a32b-a3141f513043","ttft_stream_ms":723,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1003,"queued_turn_count":0}

